(2606736, 356712, 15305, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by crayon:</b></div><hr/><i> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=361407" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/15305/thumb/361407.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/15305/thumb/361407.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/15305/thumb/361407.jpg"/></a> <br/> <br/>a lovely capture (what bug is that anyway?)<br/>I''ve also seen your edited version (as shown thumbnail above).<br/>Since you asked for a comparison - the edited one definately show a stronger colour and sharpness. Might wanna try the Fuji Vivia settings on your camera, and bump the in-camera sharpening a little higher, if straight-out-of-camera is what you do :) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks Crayon, this is one of the many varieties of Shield Bug (also known as Stink Bugs) than can be found in Central America.<br/> <br/>I definitely agree with you regarding the edited version, nevertheless I prefer to do the editing with Photoshop and try to use the RAW function in the camera as much as possible. I think that the image processor inside Digital Cameras is limited and that Photoshop offers a richer variety of choices to post process.</td>', 'Originally posted by crayon:   a lovely capture (what bug is that anyway?)I''ve also seen your edited version (as shown thumbnail above).Since you asked for a comparison - the edited one definately show a stronger colour and sharpness. Might wanna try the Fuji Vivia settings on your camera, and bump the in-camera sharpening a little higher, if straight-out-of-camera is what you do :)   Thanks Crayon, this is one of the many varieties of Shield Bug (also known as Stink Bugs) than can be found in Central America. I definitely agree with you regarding the edited version, nevertheless I prefer to do the editing with Photoshop and try to use the RAW function in the camera as much as possible. I think that the image processor inside Digital Cameras is limited and that Photoshop offers a richer variety of choices to post process.', '2006-07-10 11:10:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(2606772, 357266, 58999, '<td valign="top">Wow! So much contrast straight from camera. Congrats for the ribbon. Your images keep me motivated :) Also, your entry in the flowers challenge was awesome and deserved a ribbon as well.</td>', 'Wow! So much contrast straight from camera. Congrats for the ribbon. Your images keep me motivated :) Also, your entry in the flowers challenge was awesome and deserved a ribbon as well.', '2006-07-10 11:21:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(2606774, 357251, 40819, '<td valign="top">Thank you everyone who voted for this image. As I had said in the description I had asked for this challenge a while ago and it just blows me away how so many real photographers are shooting on DPC. You can see that you can capture a really colorful and detailed image with your camera if you know how to use it. Everyone doesn''t have to be a Photoshop wizard to capture real beauty with your camera. Thanks to the people who choose the challenges and hopefully someday we will be working on Straight from the camera X challenge.<br/> <br/>For those who voted for my image, thanks. This is my highest ranking and also highest rated image since I joined DPC over a year ago. Little by little I am getting better and some of you are the reason. Thanks.<br/></td>', 'Thank you everyone who voted for this image. As I had said in the description I had asked for this challenge a while ago and it just blows me away how so many real photographers are shooting on DPC. You can see that you can capture a really colorful and detailed image with your camera if you know how to use it. Everyone doesn''t have to be a Photoshop wizard to capture real beauty with your camera. Thanks to the people who choose the challenges and hopefully someday we will be working on Straight from the camera X challenge. For those who voted for my image, thanks. This is my highest ranking and also highest rated image since I joined DPC over a year ago. Little by little I am getting better and some of you are the reason. Thanks.', '2006-07-10 11:22:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(2606801, 355978, 11895, '<td valign="top">Sharpness and DoF seem to be spot on even without pp, you have taken advantage of what your camera has to offer better than most of us know how to.</td>', 'Sharpness and DoF seem to be spot on even without pp, you have taken advantage of what your camera has to offer better than most of us know how to.', '2006-07-10 11:34:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(2606806, 355962, 34659, '<td valign="top">What a GREAT capture!  The expressions are priceless.  Well done!</td>', 'What a GREAT capture!  The expressions are priceless.  Well done!', '2006-07-10 11:36:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(2606862, 356378, 22872, '<td valign="top">I thought this was such a clever idea and figured it would ribbon for sure!<br/> <br/></td>', 'I thought this was such a clever idea and figured it would ribbon for sure! ', '2006-07-10 11:53:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(2606885, 355962, 22872, '<td valign="top">too cute!  love the little guy on the far right! <br/></td>', 'too cute!  love the little guy on the far right! ', '2006-07-10 11:58:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(2606924, 357337, 22872, '<td valign="top">looks like a great swimming area!! takes me back to when I was kid! :)<br/>(do you guys have gators where you''re at?)</td>', 'looks like a great swimming area!! takes me back to when I was kid! :)(do you guys have gators where you''re at?)', '2006-07-10 12:11:18.000000', NULL, 0),
