(2625886, 356912, 17148, '<td valign="top">:: Critique Club :: <br/> <br/>This is not a bad shot at all straight from the camera. Really the only thing I can comment on is your exposure and your composition. Exposure looks to be finelooks to be a fair amount difference in your darks and lightsobviously you would tweak these in PS and make them have more contrast. And the composition I like alsoI like the branchif you could have gotten a bit closer and a larger shot of the bird that would be betterbut if this was the closest you could get then thats all you got. Over all I think this is the best you could do for this shot for straight out of the cameragood job. <br/></td>', ':: Critique Club ::  This is not a bad shot at all straight from the camera. Really the only thing I can comment on is your exposure and your composition. Exposure looks to be finelooks to be a fair amount difference in your darks and lightsobviously you would tweak these in PS and make them have more contrast. And the composition I like alsoI like the branchif you could have gotten a bit closer and a larger shot of the bird that would be betterbut if this was the closest you could get then thats all you got. Over all I think this is the best you could do for this shot for straight out of the cameragood job. ', '2006-07-16 00:40:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(2625957, 356567, 47933, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club Viranod!<br/> <br/>I''d call this an extremely creative shot. The placement of the subject is nice and the half heart shadow was a great idea.<br/> <br/>As was mentioned, the reflection is s huge distraction. Once a voter sees that it''s hard for them to get away from it. The rocks coming to an abrupt end on the left leaves a sense of unfinishedness. Personally, I feel that if the reflection wasn''t there and the rocks were the entire background, you''d have finished pretty high. The idea itself was excellent and, as I said, very creative. Just a couple of minor distractions cost you a few points.<br/> <br/>Thanls for the opporrtunity to critique this image Viranod.<br/> <br/>Cheers - Phil</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club Viranod! I''d call this an extremely creative shot. The placement of the subject is nice and the half heart shadow was a great idea. As was mentioned, the reflection is s huge distraction. Once a voter sees that it''s hard for them to get away from it. The rocks coming to an abrupt end on the left leaves a sense of unfinishedness. Personally, I feel that if the reflection wasn''t there and the rocks were the entire background, you''d have finished pretty high. The idea itself was excellent and, as I said, very creative. Just a couple of minor distractions cost you a few points. Thanls for the opporrtunity to critique this image Viranod. Cheers - Phil', '2006-07-16 01:08:36.000000', NULL, 0),
