(2674574, 356840, 44056, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by kteach:</b></div><hr/><i> Greetings from the Critique Club!   <br/> <br/>Overall:<br/>A nice shot, well done technically for this challenge.  Shows that you have a good command of setting up the shot and not relying on post processing.</i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>kteach, thank you so much for your critique.  I agree with every point you made.  This image was shot with the intention of being post-processed.  It was an out-take from my flower challenge shots, and I only submitted it for the "straight from camera" challenge as an afterthought.  I found some irony in your last comment, as the whole question of how much to post-process has been on my mind lately.  My background is in graphic design, so I have over a decade of PS wizardry at my disposal.  I''ve only taken up photography in the last year, and I think  PS has been a crutch for me as I learn the mechanics of my camera. I''m going to challenge myself to stop relying on post-processing, and learn to  make the camera my primary tool.  Wish me luck!</td>', 'Originally posted by kteach: Greetings from the Critique Club!    Overall:A nice shot, well done technically for this challenge.  Shows that you have a good command of setting up the shot and not relying on post processing.  kteach, thank you so much for your critique.  I agree with every point you made.  This image was shot with the intention of being post-processed.  It was an out-take from my flower challenge shots, and I only submitted it for the "straight from camera" challenge as an afterthought.  I found some irony in your last comment, as the whole question of how much to post-process has been on my mind lately.  My background is in graphic design, so I have over a decade of PS wizardry at my disposal.  I''ve only taken up photography in the last year, and I think  PS has been a crutch for me as I learn the mechanics of my camera. I''m going to challenge myself to stop relying on post-processing, and learn to  make the camera my primary tool.  Wish me luck!', '2006-07-29 18:45:51.000000', NULL, 0),
